dsh-manual-approval README · Reject with the rule warning：- a rejection only — approving a warned call injects nothing;
- only when a warning was actually raised — a plain prompt has no red mark, so
  the default "no reason" sentence is unchanged;
- a reason you type always wins over the warning;
- off (the default): behaviour is exactly as before.

The sentence still comes from the same formatter as a typed reason, so the model
cannot tell the two apart.
